## 🧹 Part 3 — Keeping your Desktop clean (optional but nice)

All those shortcuts piling up on your Desktop? Hide them away — GameDock doesn't care where they live, only that they don't get deleted.

1. Press **Win + R**, type `%LOCALAPPDATA%\GameDock`, press **Enter** — this opens GameDock's own hidden folder
2. **Cut** (Ctrl+X) the game shortcuts from your Desktop and **Paste** (Ctrl+V) them into this folder
3. ⚠️ **Important:** GameDock still points at the old Desktop location, so fix each moved game:
   - Click the **✕** on its bubble to remove it
   - Click **+ Add a game**, and in the file picker type `%LOCALAPPDATA%\GameDock` in the top bar, press Enter
   - Select the shortcut from there → done ✅

> 💡 **Pro tip:** skip the mess entirely — whenever you create a new game shortcut, move it into that folder *first*, and then add it to GameDock from there.

**The golden rule:** 🚫 never delete a shortcut that a GameDock bubble uses — the bubble will stop working. Moving is fine (just re-add it), deleting is not.

---

## 📌 Part 4 — Pin GameDock to your taskbar

Make GameDock one click away, forever — and remove it from your Desktop if you like:

1. Press **Win + R**, type `%LOCALAPPDATA%\GameDock`, press **Enter**
2. Double-click the **GameDock** file that says **Application** (purple ▶ icon) — the app opens
3. **Right-click GameDock's icon on the taskbar** → **Pin to taskbar**
4. Close the app, then click the pinned icon to test — it should open ✅
5. Now you can safely **delete GameDock.exe from your Desktop** — the taskbar pin uses the hidden copy

> ⚠️ The order matters! Always start the app **from the hidden folder** before pinning — the pin remembers where the app was launched from.

---

## ❓ Quick troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| Bubble does nothing / error when clicked | The game's file or shortcut was moved or deleted. Remove the bubble (✕) and re-add the game from its new location |
| Blue "Windows protected your PC" screen | Click **More info → Run anyway** — one time only |
| Bubble shows a letter instead of game art | Normal for Steam/Xbox shortcuts — launching still works fine |
| Taskbar icon stopped working | You deleted the file it pointed to. Redo Part 4 from the hidden folder |
| Accidentally added the wrong file | Click the **✕** on the bubble and add again |

---

## 🗂️ Where GameDock keeps things (for the curious)

- **The app:** `C:\Users\YOU\AppData\Local\GameDock\GameDock.exe`
- **Your game list:** `C:\Users\YOU\AppData\Roaming\GameDock\games.txt`

Your library survives restarts, updates, and reinstalls. Uninstalling = just delete those two folders. That's the whole footprint!

